    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Log in with Jianying desktop app first, or use QR/link URL login.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --require-jianying-app \r\n                              Require installed Jianying desktop app for login.\r\n          --qr-code           Use terminal QR-code scan login flow.\r\n          --link-url          Print a browser login URL and wait for authorization.\r\n          --no-wait           Agent/LLM split-flow: return URL/QR metadata immediately without\r\n                              polling. Defaults to QR scan; combine with --link-url for browser\r\n                              link flow.\r\n          --device-code TEXT  Poll and complete a previous --no-wait link login device code.\r\n          --user-code TEXT    User code returned by a previous --no-wait link login.\r\n          --session-handoff TEXT \r\n                              Session handoff returned by a previous --no-wait link login.\r\n          --qr-token TEXT     Poll and complete a previous --qr-code --no-wait login token.\r\n          --qr-device-id TEXT Device id returned by a previous --qr-code --no-wait login.\r\n          --credential-json TEXT \r\n                              Inline credential JSON, or @path to read external credential.json\r\n                              injected by the caller (Jianying app, IDE, agent, etc.).\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Terminal/manual login: finish in-place without split-flow.\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth login\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth login --require-jianying-app\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth login --qr-code\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth login --link-url\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth login --credential-json @/tmp/credential.json\r\n\r\n  # Agent/LLM login: use split-flow, show the QR and fallback link, then finish after the user replies \"authorized\".\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth login --qr-code --no-wait\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth login --qr-token <token> --qr-device-id <device_id> --device-code <device_code> --user-code <user_code> --session-handoff <handoff>\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth login --link-url --no-wait\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth login --device-code <device_code> --user-code <user_code> --session-handoff <handoff>\r\n\r\nLEARN MORE\r\n  Terminal users should not pass --no-wait for QR/link flows; the CLI prints QR/link output and waits.\r\n  Agents/LLMs should pass --no-wait. For QR login, render qr_image_markdown\r\n  as an inline image and print fallback_login_url; tell the user QR may expire.\r\n  For link login, display the returned login_url.\r\n  Tell the user: \"Reply \\\"authorized\\\" after completing authorization, and I will continue the login flow.\",\r\n  then run the returned completion_command_args / completion_command.\r\n  Check the result with `lyra-cli auth status` or `lyra-cli auth me`.\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
      "output": "Log in with Jianying desktop app first, or use QR/link URL login.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --require-jianying-app \r\n                              Require installed Jianying desktop app for login.\r\n          --qr-code           Use terminal QR-code scan login flow.\r\n          --link-url          Print a browser login URL and wait for authorization.\r\n          --no-wait           Agent/LLM split-flow: return URL/QR metadata immediately without\r\n                              polling. Defaults to QR scan; combine with --link-url for browser\r\n                              link flow.\r\n          --device-code TEXT  Poll and complete a previous --no-wait link login device code.\r\n          --user-code TEXT    User code returned by a previous --no-wait link login.\r\n          --session-handoff TEXT \r\n                              Session handoff returned by a previous --no-wait link login.\r\n          --qr-token TEXT     Poll and complete a previous --qr-code --no-wait login token.\r\n          --qr-device-id TEXT Device id returned by a previous --qr-code --no-wait login.\r\n          --credential-json TEXT \r\n                              Inline credential JSON, or @path to read external credential.json\r\n                              injected by the caller (Jianying app, IDE, agent, etc.).\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Terminal/manual login: finish in-place without split-flow.\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth login\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth login --require-jianying-app\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth login --qr-code\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth login --link-url\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth login --credential-json @/tmp/credential.json\r\n\r\n  # Agent/LLM login: use split-flow, show the QR and fallback link, then finish after the user replies \"authorized\".\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth login --qr-code --no-wait\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth login --qr-token <token> --qr-device-id <device_id> --device-code <device_code> --user-code <user_code> --session-handoff <handoff>\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth login --link-url --no-wait\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth login --device-code <device_code> --user-code <user_code> --session-handoff <handoff>\r\n\r\nLEARN MORE\r\n  Terminal users should not pass --no-wait for QR/link flows; the CLI prints QR/link output and waits.\r\n  Agents/LLMs should pass --no-wait. For QR login, render qr_image_markdown\r\n  as an inline image and print fallback_login_url; tell the user QR may expire.\r\n  For link login, display the returned login_url.\r\n  Tell the user: \"Reply \\\"authorized\\\" after completing authorization, and I will continue the login flow.\",\r\n  then run the returned completion_command_args / completion_command.\r\n  Check the result with `lyra-cli auth status` or `lyra-cli auth me`.\r\n",
